The ASK meta-brand public landing site — a reference implementation of the
ASK design family.

This product vendors foundations and one pattern from design-system-ASK
(github.com/apexSolarKiss/design-system-ASK):
  - colors_and_type.css        — canonical tokens (Tier 1 + Tier 2)
  - fonts/                      — Inter + JetBrains Mono variable webfonts (OFL; see fonts/*-OFL.txt)
  - assets/logo-ASK.*          — the logo-ASK wordmark (ASK Tier 3)
  - surface-shell.css          — the surface-shell pattern: the shared page
                                 shell, vendored as a pinned byte-identical
                                 copy and not modified here

design-system-ASK owns the shared page shell. It governs the page container,
the header layout, the wordmark slot, the structural title and lede, the header
rule, and the footer's alignment and link interaction. This site supplies its
own Tier 3 identity into the shell's mark slot, and adds instance-specific
payload and layout adaptations around the shell — it does not add all of its
own layout, and it defines no new tokens. The homepage is the explicit
exception: it keeps its own composition and does not consume the shell.

When this site and design-system-ASK disagree on a foundation value or on the
shell, the canonical design-system-ASK file (itself downstream of ASK's
visual-identity-system.md) wins.

